[260.634636, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0msed -n '1,120p' /etc/postfix/main.cf; echo '--- mailman relevant ---'; sed -n '24,40p;240,275p' /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg\r\n# See /usr/share/postfix/main.cf.dist for a commented, more complete version\r\n\r\n\r\n# Debian specific:  Specifying a file name will cause the first\r\n# line of that file to be used as the name.  The Debian default\r\n# is /etc/mailname.\r\n#myorigin = /etc/mailname\r\n\r\nsmtpd_banner = $myhostname ESMTP $mail_name (Ubuntu)\r\nbiff = no\r\n\r\n# appending .domain is the MUA's job.\r\nappend_dot_mydomain = no\r\n\r\n# Uncomment the next line to generate \"delayed mail\" warnings\r\n#delay_warning_time = 4h\r\n\r\nreadme_directory = no\r\n\r\n# See http://www.postfix.org/COMPATIBILITY_README.html -- default to 3.6 on\r\n# fresh installs.\r\ncompatibility_level = 3.6\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n# TLS parameters\r\nsmtpd_tls_cert_file=/etc/ssl/certs/ssl-cert-snakeoil.pem\r\nsmtpd_tls_key_file=/etc/ssl/private/ssl-cert-snakeoil.key\r\nsmtpd_tls_security_level=may\r\n\r\nsmtp_tls_CApath=/etc/ssl/certs\r\nsmtp_tls_security_level=may\r\nsmtp_tls_session_cache_database = btree:${data_directory}/smtp_scache\r\n\r\n\r\nsmtpd_relay_restrictions = permit_mynetworks permit_sasl_authenticated defer_unauth_destination\r\nalias_maps = hash:/etc/aliases\r\nalias_database = hash:/etc/aliases\r\nrelayhost = \r\nmynetworks = 127.0.0.0/8 [::ffff:127.0.0.0]/104 [::1]/128\r\nmailbox_size_limit = 0\r\nrecipient_delimiter = +\r\ninet_interfaces = all\r\ninet_protocols = all\r\n\r\n# --- Mailman 3 / local.edu configuration ---\r\nmyhostname = local.edu\r\nmydomain = local.edu\r\nmyorigin = local.edu\r\nmydestination = $myhostname, localhost, localhost.localdomain, local.edu\r\n# Route list robot addresses to Mailman's LMTP server.\r\ntransport_maps = hash:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp\r\n# Accept local Unix users plus the Mailman robot addresses.\r\nlocal_recipient_maps = proxy:unix:passwd.byname $alias_maps hash:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp\r\n# Mailboxes live in /var/mail/<username> (mbox format).\r\nmail_spool_directory = /var/mail\r\n--- mailman relevant ---\r\n# This address is the \"site owner\" address.  Certain messages which must be\r\n# delivered to a human, but which can't be delivered to a list owner (e.g. a\r\n# bounce from a list owner), will be sent to this address.  It should point to\r\n# a human.\r\nsite_owner: root@local.edu\r\n\r\n# This is the local-part of an email address used in the From field whenever a\r\n# message comes from some entity to which there is no natural reply recipient.\r\n# Mailman will append '@' and the host name of the list involved.  This\r\n# address must not bounce and it must not point to a Mailman process.\r\nnoreply_address: noreply\r\n\r\n# The default language for this server.\r\ndefault_language: en\r\n\r\n# Membership tests for posting purposes are usually performed by looking at a\r\n# set of headers, passing the test if any of their values match a member of\r\n\r\n[mta]\r\n# The class defining the interface to the incoming mail transport agent.\r\n#incoming: mailman.mta.exim4.LMTP\r\nincoming: mailman.mta.postfix.LMTP\r\n\r\n# The callable implementing delivery to the outgoing mail transport agent.\r\n# This must accept three arguments, the mailing list, the message, and the\r\n# message metadata dictionary.\r\noutgoing: mailman.mta.deliver.deliver\r\n\r\n# How to connect to the outgoing MTA.  If smtp_user and smtp_pass is given,\r\n# then Mailman will attempt to log into the MTA when making a new connection.\r\nsmtp_host: localhost\r\nsmtp_port: 25\r\nsmtp_user:\r\nsmtp_pass:\r\n\r\n# Where the LMTP server listens for connections.  Use 127.0.0.1 instead of\r\n# localhost for Postfix integration, because Postfix only consults DNS\r\n# (e.g. not /etc/hosts).\r\nlmtp_host: 127.0.0.1\r\nlmtp_port: 8024\r\n\r\n# Where can we find the mail server specific configuration file?  The path can\r\n# be either a file system path or a Python import path.  If the value starts\r\n# with python: then it is a Python import path, otherwise it is a file system\r\n# path.  File system paths must be absolute since no guarantees are made about\r\n# the current working directory.  Python paths should not include the trailing\r\n# .cfg, which the file must end with.\r\n#configuration: pyt"]
[260.634808, "o", "hon:mailman.config.exim4\r\nconfiguration: python:mailman.config.postfix\r\n"]
[261.928426, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mmailq 2>&1 | tail -20; echo '--- mailman status ---'; su -s /bin/bash list -c 'mailman -C /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg status' 2>&1; echo '--- ports ---'; ss -ltn | grep -E ':25|:8024|:8001'; echo '--- members ---'; su -s /bin/bash list -c 'mailman -C /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg members reading-group@local.edu' 2>&1\r\nMail queue is empty\r\n--- mailman status ---\r\nGNU Mailman is running (master pid: 5654)\r\n--- ports ---\r\n/bin/bash: line 1: ss: command not found\r\n--- members ---\r\nreading-group.local.edu has no members\r\n"]
[263.027949, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[285.539287, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0m/etc/init.d/postfix restart >/tmp/postfix_restart.log 2>&1; /etc/init.d/mailman3 restart >/tmp/mailman_restart.log 2>&1; sleep 6; cat /tmp/postfix_restart.log; cat /tmp/mailman_restart.log; /etc/init.d/postfix status 2>&1; su -s /bin/bash list -c 'mailman -C /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg status' 2>&1; cd /app && python3 eval.py >/tmp/eval_restart.log 2>&1; rc=$?; tail -n 8 /tmp/eval_restart.log; echo EXIT:$rc\r\npostfix/postlog: stopping the Postfix mail system\r\n   ...done.\r\npostfix/postlog: starting the Postfix mail system\r\n   ...done.\r\n * Restarting Mailman3 program mailman3\r\nStarting Mailman's master runner\r\nGenerating MTA alias maps\r\n   ...done.\r\n * postfix is running\r\nGNU Mailman is running (master pid: 6253)\r\n\r\nOr you should include the following line -- and only the following\r\nline -- in a message to reading-group-request@local.edu:\r\n\r\n    confirm cd2a0b5e44680b79b6...\r\nReply to reading-group-confirm+cd2a0b5e44680b79b6226f1c523202a282a51e76@local.edu from 8146bc53249d1fed@local.edu for join\r\nRetrying in 2 seconds...\r\n8146bc53249d1fed has confirmed their subscription\r\nEXIT:0\r\n"]
[287.342711, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[289.453787, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0msu -s /bin/bash list -c 'mailman -C /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg delmembers -l reading-group@local.edu -a -G -N' >/dev/null 2>&1; for u in $(getent passwd | awk -F: '$1 ~ /^[0-9a-f]{16}$/ {print $1}'); do userdel \"$u\" 2>/dev/null || true; rm -f \"/var/mail/$u\"; done; echo 'members:'; su -s /bin/bash list -c 'mailman -C /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg members reading-group@local.edu' 2>&1; echo 'mailboxes:'; ls -la /var/mail; echo 'queue:'; mailq 2>&1 | tail -3\r\nmembers:\r\nreading-group.local.edu has no members\r\nmailboxes:\r\ntotal 12\r\ndrwxrwsr-x 1 root mail 4096 Nov  1 00:27 .\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root 4096 Apr  4  2025 ..\r\nqueue:\r\nMail queue is empty\r\n"]
[290.910896, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[294.133968, "o", "Mail server is set up and running.\r\n\r\nWhat I configured:\r\n- **Mailman** in `/etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg`\r\n  - `[mta]` uses Postfix LMTP on `127.0.0.1:8024`\r\n  - Site owner set to `root@local.edu`\r\n- **Postfix** in `/etc/postfix/main.cf`\r\n  - Handles `local.edu` as a local domain\r\n  - Routes `reading-group*@local.edu` to Mailman via `/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp`\r\n  - Delivers user mail to `/var/mail/<username>` as mbox\r\n- **Mailing list** `reading-group@local.edu`\r\n  - `subscription_policy = open` (no owner approval; new addresses still confirm)\r\n  - `unsubscription_policy = confirm` (users must reply to confirm leaving)\r\n  - Posts are accepted without moderator approval\r\n  - Join/leave/subscribe/unsubscribe/confirm aliases generated\r\n\r\nVerified:\r\n- Direct mail delivery to `/var/mail/<user>`\r\n- Join request → confirmation mail → confirmed subscription\r\n- Posting to `reading-group@local.edu` delivered to all subscribers\r\n- Leave request → confirmation mail → removal, with remaining subscribers still receiving posts\r\n\r\nBoth `postfix` and `mailman3` are currently running. The list was left with no test members.\r\n"]
[294.36358, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@524e0b88447d:/app# "]
